---
/**
 * Card for a diagram.
 *
 * A diagram never shrinks below the width where its labels stop being
 * readable: squeezing a 900-unit viewBox into a 375px phone renders 12px text
 * at under 4px. Below that floor it scrolls sideways inside the card, the same
 * way the results table does — what must never scroll horizontally is the page.
 *
 * `min-w-0` is what makes that true. Grid and flex items default to
 * `min-width: auto`, which refuses to shrink below the content: without it the
 * floor below pushes its whole grid track wide and the PAGE scrolls instead of
 * the card.
 */
---

<div class="min-w-0 rounded-card bg-surface p-6 sm:p-12">
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <div class="min-w-[52rem]">
      <slot />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
